    "news": {
      "added": [
        {
          "id": 3428,
          "title": "Call for Participants in the PSD Technical Community and Kick-off Announcement",
          "announcement": "<p>The National Information Assurance Partnership/Common Criteria Evaluation and Validation Scheme (NIAP/CCEVS) is pleased to invite interested parties to be part of a Technical Community (TC) for the update of the Protection Profile for Peripheral Sharing Device (PSD), Version 5.0.</p>\r\n<p>The purpose of this update is to:</p>\r\n<ul type=\"disc\">\r\n<li>Update testing;</li>\r\n<li>Transition to the latest version of the Common Criteria, CC:2022; and</li>\r\n<li>Incorporate applicable Technical Decisions (TDs).</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p>The PSD TC kick-off meeting will be held on <strong>Thursday, September 10th, from 10:00-11:00am EDT</strong>. A meeting invitation will be sent to the TC alias.</p>\r\n<p>Additional Information:</p>\r\n<p>- All interested parties should apply to the PSD TC by navigating to the <a href=\"https://www.niap-ccevs.org/technical-communities\">Technical Communities page</a>&nbsp;on the NIAP website and click \"Become A US Technical Community Participant\".</p>\r\n<p>- If you are already a member of the PSD TC, there is no need to re-apply.</p>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p>Thank you for your interest and we look forward to your participation.</p>",
